            "FIX"
        },

    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.0",
    date = "Nov 4, 2026",
    title = "Charms, matchmaking and buff rotations",
    items = {
        {
            "🔮",
            "Simulator card",
            "Home tab: what the simulator expects of the run you're playing (a win or a loss, and at which wave), how the run is going against that at the start of every wave (ahead, on track or behind), how your units stand and why, the lane, and who does the damage. In the lobby, what it reads for the next mode.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "💍",
            "Smart Charm Equip",
            "Summer Charms give bonuses in the Summer Hunt and Sky Portals, one worn at a time. Before either, the farm puts on the one that helps most: more rewards where your team wins with room to spare, more damage where it might lose. Charms only change in the lobby, so a replay goes through it once when a better one is waiting. Farm → Events.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🤝",
            "Matchmaking in every mode that has it",
            "Farm → Party: a switch for each mode the game matchmakes. The Daily (on, as before), raids (up to 6 players), Infinite and Legend Stages (up to 4) and the Summer Hunt (up to 6). Other players' units help, and outside the Daily the enemies get tougher with each player. If nobody joins in time, it plays alone.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🎶",
            "Buffs that stack keep stacking",
            "Windsong's buff adds up: +30% with one, +69% with two, +100% with three. The farm used to fire its buffers whenever units needed one, so they went off together and ran out together, and your units sat at +30% most of the time. Now the copies take turns, one every few seconds, so as many buffs stay up as your copies can hold (6 Windsongs: +100%). It learns which buffers stack from its own readings. Windsong buffs magic units only.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🛣️",
            "Portals on one lane",
            "A portal tier can open on fewer lanes than its map has, and the game picks which each match. Units used to be placed for every lane, so some stood where no enemy came. Now the farm waits for the first enemies, places on their lane only, and its first unit goes down sooner.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🌪️",
            "Portal weaknesses",
            "A portal's weakness (Air Weakness x1.5) counted as no bonus at all, and air is only ever a unit's second type. Now the bonus counts for every unit that deals that type, so the team search can bring them.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "👥",
            "The team search sees buffers",
            "Units whose worth goes to the rest of the team, like buffers, Zombie (Risen)'s blessing on summons and a Gale over the road, are now tried in every slot of the team search. They used to rank by their own damage and were mostly never tried.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🎯",
            "Portals you can win go first",
            "A portal you hold used to go first whatever its chances. Now only one the simulator gives 25% or more, or one your team has already won, goes ahead of other modes.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🏃",
            "Training checks the real tier",
            "Takedown training checked its swap on a portal's plain level, not its tier's tougher enemies. Now it checks the tier it will play.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🌠",
            "Starfall",
            "In the Summer Hunt's Starfall weather, Star Golems fall in, and the simulator didn't play them. Now each Starfall run counts them, and the simulator adds them from then on.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📨",
            "Reports go out once",
            "A match record or study report could be sent twice when a study run went to the lobby right after its match. Now the farm saves at once that it went.",
            "FIX"
        },

        {
            "⚔️",
            "A study's last wave",
            "On a study run's last wave the whole team now fights.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🔁",
            "Matchmaking every run",
            "With a mode's matchmaking switch on, the farm goes back to the lobby and matchmakes again after every run. A replay used to start the next run alone, without the players who'd joined.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🧱",
            "Buffers in a block",
            "A buffer that stacks is now worth the step its copies make together: Windsong +30% with 2 copies, +69% with 4, +100% with 6. The farm used to stop at 3 and hold +30%. Now it puts the block down early, next to your main damage dealers.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "📅",
            "The Daily with others",
            "When the simulator says your team can't win the Daily alone, the farm plays it only with other players: if nobody joins, it tries matchmaking again in 10 minutes instead of losing it alone. On the morning this came in, 11 of 11 Dailies played alone were lost and 5 of 5 played with others were won. With Matchmake The Daily off, it waits for a team that can win it.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🌀",
            "Play Portals You Can't Beat",
            "Farm → Stages: your portals go first even when the simulator says your team will lose there. Off by default.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🔄",
            "Your other portals",
            "When the portal kind you picked runs out (or Only Portals finds nothing on Smart), the farm plays your other portals, best first, instead of waiting.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🎭",
            "Summer skins counted once",
            "In the Summer Hunt the game already puts a Summer skin's damage boost into the unit's damage, and the simulator added it a second time. A Spirit Reaper in its +5000% skin read 51 times too strong, and Hunts the simulator called wins were lost at wave 13-24. Now it counts once.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
